# `step:together`'s control (tflw `G1`, `D1381`). `together-met.tflw` without its `together` line:
# the row with no setup reaches `/gate` 2.5 s before the other, waits out the gate's 1.5 s alone, and
# the second arrives to an empty gate. Both rows pass, so the only thing that moves between the two
# files is whether anybody was ever in the gate at the same time as somebody else.

with each concurrently
  | wait |
  | 0    |
  | 2500 |
test "row {wait} races for the gate"
  wait until api GET /after/{wait}
    expect status equals 200
  api GET /gate
  expect status equals 200
